{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mr6ce97il7j","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"daemon idle cpu final fix uncached buildGraph hammered by label drain","summary":"FOLLOW-UP to note:note-mr6bu1tyaaa (daemon cpu hot loop write path starvation). After the per-task-loop indexes (judgingState, depRefs, harnessTranscript) and the per-tick drain-overlay cache landed, the write path was fixed (0.00s) but idle CPU still sat at ~75%. Two further fixes closed it: (1) overlay.blockingEdgeSet + an O(1) hasBlockingEdge fast path threaded via opts.blockingSet, removing the last O(tasks x edges) build scan (isReversePairedJudgeBlockingEdge per inbound edge per task). (2) THE DECISIVE ONE: buildGraph was UNCACHED while ~50 route handlers (/task/detail, /label, /judge, /git, /graph, /analytics) called it directly, each running a full O(tasks) projection per HTTP call; only readGraphSnapshot (2 callers) had a cache. The label drain's scripts/gate-label.js child fires ~220 /task/detail probes per tick, so ~220 fresh projections per label tick kept the daemon pegged even idle (a pure-idle CPU profile attributed ~92% to buildGraph under HTTP handlers). Fix: move the mtime-keyed snapCache INTO buildGraph itself (buildGraphUncached does the real projection + first-seen/adoption effects; buildGraph caches on overlayStamp = overlay file mtime). A stable overlay serves the cached projection so the 220 label probes now share ONE build; any write goes through overlayStore.save which bumps the overlay mtime, invalidating the cache so the next build is fresh. Safe because every caller treats the graph read-only (g.tasks.map/iterate, no push/sort/reassign) and readGraphSnapshot already shared one cached graph across callers. RESULT: idle CPU 100-140% flat peg -> genuine 0.0% idle between drain events (spikes only on actual writes/requests); write latency 5-20s+ -> 0.00s; all health endpoints sub-second. 6 commits on branch orch/attempt/codex-daemon-cpu-hot-loop-write-path-starvation-investigation-fix. Files: daemon.js, lib/judge.js, lib/headless-drain.js, lib/overlay.js, test/judging-gate.test.js.","category":null,"tags":[],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-07-04T12:32:30.750Z","vec":[-0.07369089126586914,0.00025407105567865074,-0.03168924152851105,0.05259287729859352,0.038758981972932816,-0.13710002601146698,0.019200043752789497,0.00623295595869422,0.026549765840172768,0.08992661535739899,-0.012696492485702038,0.018143851310014725,-0.013651121407747269,-0.05908779799938202,-0.025550559163093567,0.008440492674708366,0.09639813005924225,-0.07442069798707962,-0.04746144264936447,-0.06386899948120117,0.02016378939151764,-0.015414326451718807,0.04409650340676308,0.02166900970041752,0.039982233196496964,0.026035036891698837,-0.10314665734767914,-0.036466892808675766,-0.0023372911382466555,-0.008982042782008648,-0.02122335135936737,0.0219667199999094,-0.06369736045598984,-0.006609523203223944,0.010365843772888184,0.10212965309619904,-0.02646244503557682,-0.01634843647480011,-0.043338388204574585,0.013127322308719158,0.013514963909983635,0.09742718935012817,-0.027687305584549904,0.0047971103340387344,-0.037565216422080994,-0.028132909908890724,-0.08158120512962341,-0.043196696788072586,-0.1156487837433815,-0.01628969982266426,-0.02299470454454422,-0.030475826933979988,-0.004771464504301548,-0.02328062616288662,0.07180885970592499,0.03738531842827797,0.02500617504119873,-0.0035320634488016367,-0.0420537106692791,0.056253984570503235,-0.012981978245079517,0.015044283121824265,-0.02191433496773243,-0.04252128675580025,0.08189915120601654,0.030165866017341614,0.09100537747144699,-0.04586186632514,0.054819170385599136,0.02909943275153637,0.021832769736647606,0.05533820018172264,-0.04648490250110626,-0.07536356896162033,0.024723773822188377,0.03987147659063339,0.001820671372115612,0.005934848915785551,0.00013831093383487314,-0.20049947500228882,-0.03457561135292053,-0.010166053660213947,-0.006571481470018625,-0.009070917032659054,0.0007847858942113817